3. Hypothalamus, olfactory bulbs and spinal cord are simple approximations generated by
   the build script at standard MNI positions.

Receptor structure (6CM4.pdb.gz, d2-poses.json): built by tools/build_receptor.py from three
entries of the RCSB Protein Data Bank (https://www.rcsb.org):

1. 6CM4: human D2 dopamine receptor with risperidone, X-ray (Wang S, et al. Nature
   2018;555:269-273). Receptor residues and risperidone only; the T4 lysozyme fusion,
   waters and crystallization additives are removed. Gzip-compressed.
2. 6LUQ: D2 receptor with haloperidol, X-ray (Fan L, et al. Nat Commun 2020;11:1074).
   Haloperidol coordinates, superposed onto 6CM4 on transmembrane Cα atoms.
3. 8U02: D2 receptor with dopamine and Gαo, cryo-EM (Nat Commun 2024;15:6643). Dopamine
   coordinates and the active-state positions of receptor atoms that move on activation,
   superposed onto 6CM4 on the TM1-TM4 Cα atoms.

